  The reel_script and slides say the parole was given 'on the orders' or as a concession by Chief Minister Vijay (முதல்வர் விஜய் சலுகை), but the article only asks why Chief Minister Vijay gave the concession as a question; it does not state that Vijay granted the parole.
  The reel_script says the parole for the Coimbatore blast convicts is a concession given to those who targeted Advani ('அத்வானியை குறிவைத்தவர்களுக்கும் இந்தச் சலுகை வழங்கப்பட்டுள்ளதாக'), mixing two groups; the article does not clearly establish that the 5 paroled convicts are the same people who targeted Advani.
  The reel_script states 'விமர்சனங்கள் எழுந்துள்ளன' (criticism has arisen), which is not stated in the article beyond the question 'why'.
  The reel_script and slides say Muthuramalinga Thevar's statue was garlanded in Coimbatore Kurichi 'by the public', and the reel says a Coimbatore district collector's farmers' camp was held, but the article's Coimbatore farmer item lacks the detail; the reel_script attributes the Tiruppur collector speech to the Tiruppur event, which is supported, but the slide 'கோவை மரியாதை' is consistent. Main issue: the reel_script omits the article's key fact of the Tiruppur-related Devar Jayanti event at Mangalam Road and the Tiruppur collector's name is attributed only in part.
  The caption states the Coimbatore blast convict parole was granted and that the question of why Chief Minister Vijay gave the concession 'arose' as a conclusion, and it wrongly frames the concession as given to Advani's targeters without the article supporting that link.
